At Wed, 28 Dec 2005 16:05:12 -0600,
David Smoot wrote:
> 
> Thanks to the help of the list I've made a lot of progress.  I'm getting a new error
> message now when I attempt any capture or playback:
> ALSA lib timer_hw.c:269:(snd_timer_hw_open) extended read is not supported
> (SNDRV_TIMER_IOCTL_TREAD)
> 
> I've got the timer device created (/dev/snd/timer, owner root, group audio,
> permissions 666, character device with major of 116 and minor 33).  I'm trying to find
> info from the API docs on alsa-project.org but no luck so far.
> 
> I see in /usr/share/alsa/alsa.conf it sets some default timer values:
> defaults.timer.class 2
> defaults.timer.sclass 0
> defaults.timer.card 0
> defaults.timer.device 0
> defaults.timer.subdevice 0
> 
> But I have no idea what these mean or where they are documented.  Can someone point me
> to an expanation of the alsa.conf values?

The values above have likely nothing to do with your error.
The timer is used in dmix/dsnoop code, and the values are hardcoded.

You should disable the default dmix/dsnoop setup at first.


Takashi


